Thanks for your patience, @jeremyFreeAgent. Rebased on 8.2 and applied the two review points that were still open.

@94noni was right about `X-Debug-Token-Link`: `WebDebugToolbarListener` already generates exactly the same absolute URL, same route, same token, same `ABSOLUTE_URL`, and stores it in that header. The listener now reads it instead of regenerating it, so the `UrlGenerator` dependency is gone from both the class and the service definition, and there is one source of truth. It also inherits that listener's error handling for free, since a failing generation there sets `X-Debug-Error` and leaves the header unset.

That makes ordering matter, so the priority is now -2049 instead of -2048, one below `WebDebugToolbarListener`, rather than relying on registration order. A test asserts the relationship rather than the number.

@GromNaN's point is in as well: the message is now interpolated by the logger, `'See profiler at {profiler_url}'` with the URL in the context, instead of being built with `sprintf()`.

On your own question about folding this into the existing `RESPONSE` log line: I would keep the separate line. Doing it on `RESPONSE` needs a Monolog processor or formatter, which ties WebProfilerBundle to Monolog specifics and only works for handlers using that format, whereas a debug-level line on the `profiler` channel works with any handler and costs nothing in dev. Happy to be overruled.

Tests rewritten around the header, including one that fails if the header name changes. WebProfilerBundle is green at 180 tests.

