by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-14T07:07:17Z

Correction to my previous comment, and an answer to whether this belongs in `WebDebugToolbarListener`: no, and reading `X-Debug-Token-Link` was wrong too. I reverted that part.

`WebProfilerExtension::load()` only loads `toolbar.php` when `toolbar.enabled` or `intercept_redirects` is set:

```php
if ($config['toolbar']['enabled'] || $config['intercept_redirects']) {
    $loader->load('toolbar.php');
```

So with the toolbar off, `WebDebugToolbarListener` does not exist, nothing sets `X-Debug-Token-Link`, and both folding the logging into that listener and reading its header would silently log nothing. That is backwards for this feature: a profiler link in the logs is most useful exactly where the toolbar is useless, on API responses and other non-HTML traffic, which is also where people turn the toolbar off.

So the listener stays separate, registered from `profiler.php` which is always loaded, and generates the URL itself as you originally wrote it. The duplication @94noni pointed at is one `generate()` call, and it is the price of not depending on the toolbar; there is a comment in the code saying so. The priority goes back to -2048 since there is no ordering dependency any more.

@GromNaN's interpolation stays, that part was a real improvement and had not actually been applied on the previous head.

Also removed a stray blank line the rebase left under the 7.3 heading in the changelog. WebProfilerBundle is green at 180 tests, and dropping the `{profiler_url}` placeholder fails the new test.
